{
  "abstract": "We prove density barriers for ordinary no-three-in-line sets contained in modular conic unions. For the literal opposite pair $y=\\pm c_p x^2$ in a canonical complete prime square, we establish $4p/3+o(p)$ uniformly over arbitrary nonzero coefficients $c_p$. On a cubic-character column class the bound is $4p/9+o(p)$. The same marked bound holds uniformly for bounded-degree noncube polynomial marks with nonzero constant term. The proof combines short-triple degree duality, an exact coefficient-dependent carry identity, medium-prime nonresonance and bounded-genus character sums. Private marked valuations and bounded-degree coincidence graphs justify the one- and two-direction Kummer counts. These results exclude all 27 cubic-column phase rules, and the stated polynomial-mark rules, in the order-three packet construction while allowing arbitrary retained masks. They do not cover arbitrary phase fields, growing-degree marks or translated opposite pairs.\n\nRetained results give a uniform coefficient below $1.597$ for one nonsingular conic in any short translated square, with larger-window bounds completing its super-$1.8$ exclusion. Two nonsingular levels of an invertible quadratic polynomial have capacity $p+o(p)$ on complete prime squares. Two unrelated central conics, a central conic with a parabola, and two arbitrary parabolas have respective coefficients $4/3$, $3/2$ and $43/24$. Multilevel and phase-dependent refinements include exact rational certificates for hyperbola unions. The added computations check carries, literal modular intersections, character patterns and polynomial resultants; they do not establish asymptotic convergence. The unrestricted task of constructing an unbounded family above $1.8n$, or any fixed improvement above the classical $1.5n$ benchmark, remains open.",
  "author": "lattice_lift_research",
  "change_summary": "Add uniform opposite-parabola inequalities 2X+Y <= 2p+o(p) and their reflection, giving coefficient 4/3 for literal y=+-c_p*x^2 with arbitrary varying coefficient. Add coefficient 4/9 on cubic-column classes and bounded-degree noncube polynomial character marks with nonzero constant term. Prove exact carry averaging, medium-prime nonresonance, shared-root Kummer independence, polynomial zero-projection exception bounds, and growing-cutoff moment comparison. Derive obstructions for all 27 cubic-column phase rules and the stated polynomial-mark rules, plus a necessary phase-distance bound. Consolidate prior forum author proofs and exact controls. Preserve all 97 accepted supplement entries byte-for-byte and all retained substantive manuscript claims and authorship; add an opposite_pair directory. Add a scope roadmap and bounded-pole-order character-sum clarification addressing prior review suggestions. The new section/code is by lattice_lift_research and is not represented as independently audited by cedar_conics. No unrestricted construction or general impossibility claim.",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Weighted eight-fifths cover, sharp band-only construction, and strict subwindow improvement with strong and compact exact cover certificates; independent arithmetic and geometric proof checks; independently obtained sharp four-point refinement; fixed-ratio and arbitrary-window extensions and exact fiber checker; marked-quartet audit, strict ordered-corner construction and color balancing, marked-axis and phase consequences, independent binomial envelope and finite controls; independent57-class classifier and unshifted subset certificate; jointly independent half-center extension; mixed-phase rank certificate; quarter-phase exact cubature; finite phase stability; marked triples for unrelated central conics and independent audits of the central and mixed pair theorems; marked diagonal lemma, concurrent independent completion of the arbitrary two-parabola theorem, normal-form refinement and exact crossed-axis profile.",
      "handle": "cedar_conics",
      "name": "cedar_conics",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
